node_modules
.git
.output
dist
*.log
.env*

# Runtime state, never build input. `COPY . .` in the build stage was uploading
# data/credentials.json — an operator credential store held in cleartext — into
# the ACR build service on every deploy. The runtime stage copies only .output,
# so it never reached the published image, but there is no reason to send it.
# data/social_cache.json* is fabricated records mentioning real individuals and
# is barred from leaving this machine (DPDP Act 2023) for the same reason
# .gitignore blocks it.
data/

# ai-service/ is a separate Python backend (vision/forensics) that deploys on its
# own, to a different host, via its own Dockerfile — never part of the frontend
# image. Without this, `COPY . .` below would upload its vendored model weights
# (~650MB when populated) to the ACR build service on every frontend deploy, the
# same class of mistake data/credentials.json made before it was excluded above.
ai-service/

# osint-workers/ is the self-hosted OSINT tool stack (SpiderFoot, theHarvester,
# SearXNG, IVRE). It runs locally in WSL via its own docker-compose, on its own
# host, and is never part of the frontend image — same reason ai-service/ and
# data/ are excluded above. Without this, `COPY . .` would upload the whole
# stack into the ACR build service on every frontend deploy.
osint-workers/
